# The local kind overlay's credentials, copied from k8s/secrets.example.yaml.
# The example is tracked; the copy never is.
k8s/secrets.yaml

# CI plants deliberate violations to prove each guard still fails, and each step removes
# its own file. A `planted_*` file that reaches a commit is one that escaped — which
# happened once, because the simulation ran every step in one shell and each step's
# `trap ... EXIT` replaced the previous one, so only the last cleanup fired. Ignoring the
# pattern means the mistake cannot reach a commit again.
services/api/**/planted_*.go
